title Caravan replace -- a run may correct a phase in one act, and both triples read the record that holds neither
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first from the running thread, Standfast on reds first, send it signed to both remotes.
think Standfast first. Walked crux/REDS.md living rows 80, 83, 84, 85 and every closed prose note. REDS #80's booked count-guard loom exists and runs GREEN on metal -- 80 crypto/*.rye files, each registered in the suite and each registration naming a real file, a bijection rather than a tally. #81, #84, #85 carry CLOSED; #82 and #86 fixed and released in-round. No open agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue opens honestly.
think Verified rather than assumed one suspicious thing: work-in-progress/ still resolves and holds byte-identical copies of REMEMBER, REDS, CAIRNS, ROADMAP, TASKS, THREADS. Inode and stat say it is a symlink to crux/, a deliberate compatibility shim git ignores. Single-strandedness holds and no red is owed. Measurement beats memory -- a diff alone would have read as a duplicate living pin.
think Council rota by lap index: 479 logs on disk, so item 21, ORGANIZING.md. Deep-read whole. Its shape test -- read the piece aloud and ask what it is doing -- is what placed this round's prose: the finding into caravan/README.md beside its siblings, the reasoning here, nothing new into context/.
think The running thread is unambiguous. The withdraw log's recommend named its own successor: a run may now grow and prune, yet a plan can be corrected only by doing both in sequence, which briefly leaves the record holding neither the old phase nor the new. So the crux is replace -- whether a run may correct a phase in one act.
think Read withdraw.rye, enlist.rye, arrive.rye, arrange.plan_is_seated, and precede.turns_are_sound before writing a line. The mechanics that mattered: arrival_admits weighs a newcomer's step against how many steps of its turn already stand; turns_are_sound holds follows_turns strictly below turn_bit(turn), so a phase may name only turns beneath its own; plan_is_seated refuses any phase naming a turn that stands after it.
think The finding fell out of those three read together. A correction that keeps a phase's turn and its step -- the commonest correction there is -- is refused by any record still holding the phase it replaces, because that record counts one step of the turn already standing while the newcomer offers step zero. The door closes on the very change it exists to make. Both triples want the residue: the record holding neither the departing phase nor the newcomer.
think Second finding, and the one that makes a sequence genuinely unsafe rather than merely untidy: the residue is a lawful plan. It seats itself, orders itself, and answers every reading a supervisor knows how to ask, so nothing in the machinery can tell a half-finished correction from a finished one. A run in that gap admits from behind the empty slot a child the correction would have held.
think Third, the refusal this rung earns on its own. A newcomer can be lawful at the tail of the residue and unlawful in the slot, since a high turn dropped into an early place names a turn standing after it. ReplacementUnseated is that fact. Chose to name it rather than fold it into ArrivalUnseated because an operator meets it in a different place than the arrival leg.
think Wrote the pure API first and kept the supervisor a faithful copy of the rung below with exactly one act added after each reaping, so the difference a reader must hold is one function rather than a rewritten loop.
obs A correction moves nothing, in the strongest form this arc has reached. A withdrawal keeps the record's length and leaves a hole; an enlistment keeps every index and grows the tail. A correction does neither -- the length never changes and no index is added -- so every child already started keeps the slot, the line, and the grants it was handed.
obs Caught and fixed a real sloppiness before the first run: three selftest sites used the turn number where an index was wanted. They coincide in this lap because turn N stands at index N, so every check would have passed for the wrong reason. Replaced each with depart's own answer, which is the honest source of a slot.
obs Both RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN was claimed. Weighing the arrival against the record still holding the phase reds at "a phase nobody waits on was refused its correction" -- the finding shown as a failure, which is the most convincing form it has. Dropping the slot's seating check seats a phase naming a turn behind it.
obs The limit is named plainly rather than left for a reader to discover: a correction reaches only work still waiting. Whether a run may correct a phase a child is running -- the work in flight finishing under the shape it started with while the record already reads the new one -- is the next rung's question.
obs Docs stayed synced in the same round: withdraw's own README limit line said the replace question belonged to the vision room until a witness binds it, and a witness now binds it, so it points at the rung below instead.
loom witness=caravan_replace_witness result=GREEN tests_per_correction=32 tests_per_seating=256 places_moved_one_act=0 places_moved_by_sequence=5 plan_len=7 children_whole=7 children_corrected=7 record_places=7 corrections_in_flight=1 named_turns_broken=0
file caravan/replace.rye the rung -- residue, replacement_refusal, replace, places_moved, and a supervisor whose record may be rewritten in place
file tools/caravan_replace_witness.rish the witness, reading the selftest natively with contains
file caravan/README.md the Replace section beside its siblings, and withdraw's limit line synced to the rung that answers it
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moved forward, the prior edge condensed to a pointer
recommend keep-going the honest next crux is the one this rung named its own limit -- a correction reaches only work still waiting, so a phase a child is running cannot be rewritten at all; the question becomes whether a record may carry two shapes of one phase at once, the work in flight finishing under the shape it started with while every reading downstream already answers from the new one, which wants a lap measuring what a run owes a child whose own declaration has already been replaced beneath it.
